30824:
Put g(x) = f(\frac{1}{x}) so that f(x) - 6g(x) = \frac{35}{3x} - \frac{5}{2}
Replace x by \frac{1}{x} to get the companion equation g(x) - 6f(x) = \frac{35x}{3} - \frac{5}{2}
Rearrange the companion as g(x) = 6f(x) + \frac{35x}{3} - \frac{5}{2} to eliminate g(x)
Substitute into the first equation to get -35f(x) = \frac{35}{3x} + 70x - \frac{35}{2}, i.e. f(x) = -2x - \frac{1}{3x} + \frac{1}{2}
Then \frac{1}{\alpha x} + f(x) = (\frac{1}{\alpha} - \frac{1}{3})\frac{1}{x} - 2x + \frac{1}{2} has a finite limit at 0 only when \frac{1}{\alpha} - \frac{1}{3} = 0
Hence \alpha = 3 and the limit is \beta = \frac{1}{2}, giving \alpha + 2\beta = 3 + 1 = 4 matching option C → (C)

30826:
Factor numerator 2^{x + 2} + 16 = 4(2^{x} + 4) and denominator 2^{2x + 1} + 2^{x + 4} + 32 = 2(2^{x} + 4)^{2}
Cancel to get f(x) = \frac{2}{2^{x} + 4} in lowest terms
Pair terms about 4: with t = 2^{x}, f(4 - x) = \frac{t}{2(t + 4)} so f(x) + f(4 - x) = \frac{4 + t}{2(t + 4)} = \frac{1}{2}
The 59 values \frac{k}{15} for k = 1 to 59 form 29 such pairs plus the middle term f(2)
Middle value f(2) = \frac{2}{4 + 4} = \frac{1}{4}, so the bracket sums to 29 \cdot \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{4} = \frac{59}{4}
Multiply by 8 to get 8 \cdot \frac{59}{4} = 118 matching option A → (A)

30827:
By Vieta \alpha + \beta = \frac{3}{2} and \alpha\beta = -i, with S_{n} = \alpha^{n} + \beta^{n} satisfying 2S_{n + 2} = 3S_{n + 1} + 2iS_{n}
Since (\alpha\beta)^{4} = (-i)^{4} = 1, subtracting (\alpha^{4} + \beta^{4})(\alpha^{15} + \beta^{15}) from the numerator leaves zero remainder
Hence the fraction collapses exactly to \alpha^{4} + \beta^{4} = S_{4}
Iterate the recurrence from S_{0} = 2 and S_{1} = \frac{3}{2} to get S_{2} = \frac{9}{4} + 2i and S_{3} = \frac{27}{8} + \frac{9i}{2}
One more step gives S_{4} = \frac{49}{16} + 9i with real part \frac{49}{16} and imaginary part 9
Product 16 \cdot \frac{49}{16} \cdot 9 = 441 matching option D → (D)

