Rewrite as \frac{dy}{dx} + \frac{x}{1 + x^{2}}y = \frac{5x^{2}}{\sqrt{1 + x^{2}}} in linear form
Integrating factor is \exp(\int \frac{x}{1 + x^{2}} \, dx) = \sqrt{1 + x^{2}}
Hence \frac{d}{dx}(y\sqrt{1 + x^{2}}) = 5x^{2} after multiplying through
Integrate to get y\sqrt{1 + x^{2}} = \frac{5x^{3}}{3} + C with C = 0 from y(0) = 0
At x = \sqrt{3} the factor is 2, so 2y(\sqrt{3}) = \frac{5 \cdot 3\sqrt{3}}{3} = 5\sqrt{3}
Thus y(\sqrt{3}) = \frac{5\sqrt{3}}{2} matching option A → (A)

30831:
Focal distances of (x_{1}, y_{1}) are a - ex_{1} and a + ex_{1}, so their product is a^{2} - e^{2}x_{1}^{2}
With x_{1} = \sqrt{3} this gives a^{2} - 3e^{2} = \frac{7}{4} as the first relation
Point on ellipse gives \frac{3}{a^{2}} + \frac{1}{4b^{2}} = 1 with b^{2} = a^{2}(1 - e^{2}) as the second relation
Write a^{2} = \frac{7}{4} + 3e^{2} and clear denominators to get 12(1 - e^{2}) + 1 = 4a^{2}(1 - e^{2})
With u = e^{2} this reduces to 12u^{2} - 17u + 6 = 0 giving u = \frac{3}{4} or u = \frac{2}{3}
Absolute difference \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} - \sqrt{\frac{2}{3}} = \frac{3 - 2\sqrt{2}}{2\sqrt{3}} matching option C → (C)

30832:
Single-throw chances are p = \frac{4}{36} = \frac{1}{9} for sum 5 and q = \frac{5}{36} for sum 8
A wins on his first throw with probability p, else play continues past one full round with probability (1 - p)(1 - q)
Summing the geometric series gives P = \frac{p}{1 - (1 - p)(1 - q)}
Substitute to get denominator 1 - \frac{8}{9} \cdot \frac{31}{36} = 1 - \frac{248}{324} = \frac{76}{324} = \frac{19}{81}
Hence P = \frac{1 / 9}{19 / 81} = \frac{9}{19}
This is option B → (B)

